Azure Portal → Storage accounts → sadsprodmigrationwest.
Left menu → Access control (IAM) → Role assignments tab.
In the Type filter, choose Apps (sometimes shown as Service principal).
Look at roles like Storage Blob Data Contributor, Contributor or Storage Account Contributor. Click each app name and check its Application (client) ID. Find the one ending in 2738.

Once have the client ID, the sequence is:
Get a new secret created. In Azure Portal, someone who owns the app (or an Entra ID admin) goes to Microsoft Entra ID → App registrations → All applications, searches the client ID, 
opens the app → Certificates & secrets → Client secrets → + New client secret, gives it a description like matillion-python-sftp and an expiry (e.g. 12 months), and clicks Add.
The secret value is shown only once, so it must be copied right away. The existing secret Matillion uses keeps working.
